<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yahya ibn Ali ibn Ghaniya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1148</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-ibn-ali">Yahya ibn Ali</a> ibn Ghaniya was an Almoravid governor and commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> during the empire's collapse in the 1140s. As local rulers set up the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdoms, he fought to hold or retake cities such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> against rebels and Christian kings. He died in 1148 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, while his brother Muhammad founded the Banu Ghaniya line in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>.</p></div>
